  "notes": "12 phases / 46 steps (S0='null step' through S45), verified against the official ontology figure (static/hierarchy.jpg) in github.com/CAMMA-public/MultiBypass140 (2026-09, repo HEAD after 'ADR-014a'), matching Lavanchy et al. 2023 (arXiv:2312.11250). Phase id = Phase_gt (from the repo's labels_by70 pickles) + 1; step id = Step_gt directly (0-based, so it round-trips with the label pickles without an offset). Several generic steps (S0 null, S3 retractor placement, S22 gastric tube placement, S39 hemostasis, S40 irrigation aspiration) recur across multiple phases in the ontology figure -> parent_phase left null (procedure_graph.step_phase_consistent treats null as always consistent) rather than picking one arbitrary phase. hard_precede: pouch creation before its anastomosis; that anastomosis before its leak test; jejunal separation before the jejunojejunal anastomosis it enables; that anastomosis before its mesenteric-defect closure. soft_precede is the rest of the canonical P1..P11 order (P12 'other intervention' is out-of-flow, no fixed position). IAE (interoperative adverse event) categories (not modeled as graph nodes): Bleeding, MechanicalInjury, ThermalInjury, IschemicInjury, InsufficientClosureOfAnastomosis, severity 0 (none) - 5."
